    "result_text": "All tests pass. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: owner `ageBand` derived from `birthDate`\n\nThe request may now include an optional `birthDate` (ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`); when present the owner response carries an `ageBand` of `MINOR` (under 18), `ADULT` (18\u201364) or `SENIOR` (65+), computed as the completed years between `birthDate` and the owner's `registrationDate`.\n\n### Files changed\n\n- **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (format `date`, optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema (the editable input), and `ageBand` (read-only string) to the `Owner` schema. The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time, so `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` pick up the new fields automatically.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) with getter/setter, and a static `ageBand(birthDate, registrationDate)` helper following the existing \"single source of truth\" pattern used by the other derived fields. Returns `null` when either date is absent.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 mapped `ageBand` to the new `formatAgeBand(owner)` helper. `birthDate` maps automatically (field now exists on both entity and DTOs), so it's persisted on create and returned unchanged.\n- **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n### Design notes\n- `ageBand` is derived on read (not stored), consistent with the other read-only derived fields (`contactPreference`, `membershipNumber`, etc.). It's computed against `registrationDate` per the spec \u2014 and since `registrationDate` defaults to the server's current date on create when omitted, the band resolves correctly for the test's case (`birthDate` 1990-01-01 \u2192 `ADULT`).\n- I kept `ageBand` as a plain string rather than an OpenAPI `enum` to match the precedent of `contactPreference` (also an enumerated-in-practice value typed as a plain string), which keeps the mapper expression returning a simple `String` and avoids a generated nested enum type.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS` (full suite).",
