    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing patterns in both files:\n\n- `Owner.ageBand(LocalDate, LocalDate)` is a static, side-effect-free derivation method taking exactly the fields it needs and returning `null` when inputs are absent \u2014 identical in shape and spirit to the neighbouring `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`, `contactPreference`, `locality`, etc. Logic lives in the domain model, which is where all the other derived-value logic already lives.\n- `OwnerMapper.formatAgeBand(Owner)` is a thin `default` adapter that null-checks the owner and delegates to the static method, matching `formatCheckDigit`, `formatContactPreference`, `formatMembershipNumber` one-for-one, and the `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(formatAgeBand(owner))\")` entry is registered the same way as its siblings.\n- The field + getter/setter, the `java.time.Period` import, the four dialect schema additions, and the OpenAPI schema/property additions are all placed consistently with the surrounding declarations.\n\nNothing is duplicated, no class is becoming a catch-all (this is exactly the kind of derived field these two units already accumulate by design), and a maintainer of this codebase would find it natural. No structural changes needed.",
